(1374,2882,'Abnormally infrequent menstruation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4172FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1375,2888,'Fractures of the femur.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4165FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1376,2891,'diarrheal illness, usually due to infection','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'151FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1377,2895,'Pathologic process consisting of a partial or complete disruption of the layers of a surgical wound.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4093FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1378,2896,'Disorders related or resulting from abuse or mis-use of opioids.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4090FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1379,2898,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4080FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1380,2899,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1381,2900,'A progressive, degenerative joint disease, the most common form of arthritis, especially in older persons. The disease is thought to result not from the aging process but from biochemical changes and biomechanical stresses affecting articular cartilage. In the foreign literature it is often called osteoarthrosis deformans.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:58',NULL,NULL,'4067FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1382,2908,'A genus of parasitic nematodes whose organisms are distributed in Central and South America. Characteristics include a smooth cuticle and an enlarged anterior end.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'4027FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1383,2910,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'4020FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1384,2912,'Movements or behaviors associated with sleep, sleep stages, or partial arousals from sleep that may impair sleep maintenance. Parasomnias are generally divided into four groups: arousal disorders, sleep-wake transition disorders, parasomnias of REM sleep, and nonspecific parasomnias. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p191)','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3998FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1385,2913,'Clinical or subclinical disturbances of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, excessive, and disorganized discharge of brain cells. Clinical manifestations include abnormal motor, sensory and psychic phenomena. Recurrent seizures are usually referred to as EPILEPSY or \"seizure disorder.\"','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3987FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1386,2914,'Fractures occurring as a result of disease of a bone or from some undiscoverable cause, and not due to trauma. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3985FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1387,2918,'Abnormal enlargement or overgrowth of the gingivae brought about by enlargement of existing cells.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1388,2921,'Conditions in which increased pressure within a limited space compromises the circulation and function of tissue within that space. Compartmentation involves mainly the leg but also involved are the forearm, arm, thigh, shoulder, and buttock. Some of the causes of increased pressure are trauma, tight dressings, hemorrhage, and exercise. Sequelae include nerve compression, paralysis, and contracture.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3959FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1389,2922,'General or unspecified diseases of the blood vessels outside the heart. It is for diseases of the peripheral as opposed to the cardiac circulation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3957FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1390,2923,'Inflammation of the lining of the abdomen and pelvis.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3953FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1391,2924,'A major deviation from normal patterns of behavior.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3950FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1392,2928,'Inflammation of a vein associated with thrombus formation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3941FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1393,2929,'Psychiatric illness or diseases manifested by breakdowns in the adaptational process expressed primarily as abnormalities of thought, feeling, and behavior producing either distress or impairment of function.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'15797FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1394,2930,'Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3937FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1395,2938,'A placenta which develops in the lower uterine segment, in the zone of dilatation, so that it covers or adjoins the internal os. Painless hemorrhage in the last trimester, particularly during the eighth month, is the most common symptom. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3920FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1396,2939,'A condition or physical state produced by the ingestion, injection or inhalation of, or exposure to a deleterious agent.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3907FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1397,2941,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'15717FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1398,2942,'Infection occurring at the site of a surgical incision.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:05:59',NULL,NULL,'3865FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1399,2945,'Anxiety disorders manifested by the development of characteristic symptoms following a psychologically traumatic event that is outside the normal range of usual human experience. Symptoms include re-experiencing the traumatic event and numbing of responsiveness to or reduced involvement with the external world.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:06:00',NULL,NULL,'3854FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1400,2949,'Onset of labor before term but after the fetus has become viable, usually sometime during the 29th through 38th week of gestation.','en',2,'2026-08-13 12:06:00',NULL,NULL,'3846FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
